MAJOR_VERSION=5
STANDARD_VERSION=3
RELEASE_VERSION=0
PRERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=10
DESCRIPTION=Clear the first full CodeQL scan of develop. The scan on the merged develop head reported 47 high or critical C and C++ findings and 2 Python findings in code the pull request had not touched. Fixed in code: the batch and write commands build their text with bounded copies instead of strcat, the Wi-Fi host layer no longer runs the host's wpa_cli, nmcli, iw or Flinstone helper in a default build (those calls go through one gate and compile in only with make WIFI_HOST_COMMANDS=1, which the build-mode sentinel now tracks so switching it rebuilds, so the in-tree Wi-Fi drivers do all Wi-Fi unless asked otherwise), a Wi-Fi interface name is checked once after discovery and a USB port name may not contain a slash, the Wi-Fi coprocessor wipes the join passphrase after the call, server file offer, send, log and permit apply the VM jail and quarantine check that write uses and read the path that was checked (resolve_path_checked refuses a path it cannot resolve completely, at every stage and for any buffer size, and an active jail refuses an input it cannot resolve; createdisk now has the same jail check as setdisk and format), and the SAE vector generator no longer prints its test PSK. The rest are recorded in the accepted-findings register with a disposition, justification and review date, and entries that matched nothing were removed.



RELEASE_DATE=2026-10-30
